CORE dfcc-only
main.c
--dfcc main --apply-loop-contracts _ --no-standard-checks --unwinding-assertions --unwind 3
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[main.loop_assigns.\d+\] line 30 Check assigns clause inclusion for loop .*: SUCCESS$
^\[main.assertion.1\] .* assertion i == n: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^\[cmp\.assigns\.\d+\] .* is assignable: FAILURE$
--
This test checks that a contract-less loop inside a *called* function does not
have its loop-local variables checked against the assigns clause of an enclosing
loop that *does* have a contract. Before the fix, the callee's loop locals
(`res`, `pa`, `pb`, `k`) were spuriously reported as not assignable. See the
discussion in model-checking/kani#4790.
